================================================================================
Licence posture
================================================================================

The complete installed Python inventory is audited in the clean delivery image.
The current Python inventory has no component blocked by this project's release
policy. This statement does not cover the Debian operating system or all native
components: their separate licences, notices and source references are retained
in third_party/runtime/ and in the original image locations.

Frontend full licence texts and dependency notice supplements are retained in
third_party/frontend/, with original upstream notices preserved. Font notices are
retained alongside the fonts. Montserrat uses SIL OFL 1.1; its full text is at
frontend/out/vendor/fonts/LICENSE-Montserrat.txt.

The standalone agent skill archive has its own applicable NOTICE and a copy of the
Apache-2.0 LICENSE. It does not bundle the application's third-party runtime.

Native notice supplements
-------------------------
third_party/native/ retains release-specific Cargo dependency notices for the
unmodified cryptography, bcrypt, pydantic-core, watchfiles and jiter wheels,
including optional/build/platform components, plus the matching OpenSSL notice.
For multiple-licence alternatives the selected licence is recorded explicitly.
colored 3.1.1 (MPL-2.0) appears in this conservative source-lock supplement; its
full corresponding source and original licence/credits accompany the notices.
The supplement does not claim that every source-lock component is linked.
CPython's complete interpreter licence is retained in third_party/runtime/,
with its actual version and official corresponding source URL.
